Solution: Create the missing MyConfiguration.ts file at src/MyConfiguration.ts

The MyConfiguration file should export a Prisma client configuration compatible with MyGlobal.ts. This is typically a wrapper around PrismaClient with configuration options. Create a minimal implementation:

```typescript
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";

const prisma = new PrismaClient({
  log: process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" ? ["query", "error", "warn"] : ["error"],
});

export const MyConfiguration = prisma;
export default MyConfiguration;
```

This will resolve the compilation error in MyGlobal.ts and allow the authorization components to compile successfully.

